Route each UDP destination by its own rule, behind keqdroid-udp-per-exit.

tunnel.handleUDPConn keyed the NAT table by the source address alone
(packetAdapter.Key is LocalAddr), and resolveMetadata ran once, for the first
datagram of a socket. Every later datagram from that socket went out through
the same proxy whatever the rules said for its address. A game whose voice
socket first talked to an address outside the user's routes kept its voice
server on that exit, and a socket whose first datagram matched DIRECT sent
everything after it past the tunnel.

With keqdroid-udp-per-exit: true in the config, the key is the source plus the
name of the proxy the rules pick for the destination. A socket that stays on
one exit keeps one session, so P2P still sees one external port. An address
routed elsewhere gets a session of its own. The rules run once per source and
destination; the answers are kept, 65536 pairs at most.

Off by default and off without the key: P2P traffic that learns its address
from a STUN server on one exit and reaches the peer through another no longer
gets through directly (checked on a netns lab with pion ICE, 2026-10-17).

keqdroid writes the key from Settings, core settings. Applied by
tool/build_mihomo.ps1 after the other mihomo patches.

